{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp103", "text": "The supreme conqueror is not he who conquers a million men in battle, but he who conquers a single man: himself.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp103", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp104", "text": "It is surely better to conquer oneself than all those other folk. When a person has tamed themselves, always living restrained,", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp104", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp105", "text": "no god nor centaur, nor Māra nor divinity, can undo the victory of such a personage.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp105", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 16, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp144", "text": "Like a fine horse under the whip, be keen and full of urgency. With faith, ethics, and energy, immersion, and investigation of principles, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, mindful, give up this vast suffering.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp144", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity", "self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 34, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp179", "text": "He whose victory may not be undone, a victory unrivaled in all the world; by what track would you trace that Buddha, who leaves no track in his infinite range?", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp179", "chapter": "14. The Buddhas", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 30, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp190", "text": "One gone for refuge to the Buddha, to his teaching and to the Saṅgha, sees the four noble truths with right understanding:", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp190", "chapter": "14. The Buddhas", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 22, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp195", "text": "When a person venerates the worthy— the Buddha or his disciple, who have transcended proliferation, and have left behind grief and lamentation,", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp195", "chapter": "14. The Buddhas", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 22, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp201", "text": "Victory breeds enmity; the defeated sleep badly. The peaceful sleep at ease, having left victory and defeat behind.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp201", "chapter": "15. Happiness", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp217", "text": "One accomplished in virtue and vision, firmly principled, and truthful, doing oneself what ought be done: that’s who the people love.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp217", "chapter": "16. The Beloved", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp26", "text": "Fools and simpletons devote themselves to negligence. But the wise protect diligence as their best treasure.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp26", "chapter": "2. Diligence", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 16, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp268", "text": "You don’t become a sage by being sagelike, while still confused and ignorant. The astute one who holds the scales, taking only the best,", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp268", "chapter": "19. The Just", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp273", "text": "Of paths, the eightfold is the best; of truths, the four statements; dispassion is the best of things, and the Clear-eyed One is the best of humans.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp273", "chapter": "20. The Path", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 27, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp296", "text": "The disciples of Gotama always wake up refreshed, who day and night constantly recollect the Buddha.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp296", "chapter": "21. Miscellaneous", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 16, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp303", "text": "One who is faithful, accomplished in ethics, blessed with fame and wealth, is honored in whatever place they frequent.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp303", "chapter": "21. Miscellaneous", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 19, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "boastful", "selection": "tone=- topic=['self_praise'] (curation, not generation)"}
